"poc Build Signal, a customer feedback triage tool for early-stage product teams. Users submit feedback through an API or a web form. Each item is classified by an LLM for category, sentiment and urgency, and embedded for similarity. A weekly scheduled job clusters feedback into themes and writes a short summary of what changed and what needs attention. A dashboard shows themes, trends, urgent items, and lets users drill down to the raw feedback. Constraints: the system must run fully locally against an AWS-compatible emulator (endpoint http://localhost:4566) with no cloud spend. Target AWS services are API Gateway, Lambda, DynamoDB, EventBridge Scheduler and SES, with Postgres/pgvector for vectors. The LLM and embedding provider must be swappable between Ollama (local) and Amazon Bedrock by configuration only. Infrastructure must be defined as code and deployable to the emulator."
